const SEIZURE_AID = `<div class="warn"><b>If the patient has a seizure</b>Stay with the patient and time it. Move hard things away, cushion the head, and once the jerking stops roll her onto her side. Nothing in the mouth; don't hold her down. <strong>Call 911</strong> if it lasts more than 5 minutes, another starts before she comes round, she's hurt, has trouble breathing, doesn't wake up afterwards, or it happens in water.</div>`;
const FAINT_VS_SEIZURE = `<h3>A faint can look like a seizure</h3><p>A few seconds of jerking is common during an ordinary faint (in a classic video study, most induced faints showed it). Clues that it was a faint: it came on standing or in heat, the patient went pale and sweaty first, the jerks lasted seconds, and she was herself again within a minute or so. A seizure is more often followed by long confusion and sleepiness. Note what came before, time it, and if you can, take a phone video for her doctors.</p>`;

